{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalSeconds": 321.80199999999985,
 "totalFrames": 9654,
 "sentences": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "text": "Someone asks you for a favor.",
   "start": 3.2,
   "end": 4.666
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "text": "You don’t want to do it.",
   "start": 5.1,
   "end": 5.814
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "text": "You’re tired.",
   "start": 6.256,
   "end": 6.72
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "text": "You have your own problems.",
   "start": 7.166,
   "end": 8.236
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "text": "But before you can even think, your mouth says, ‘Of course.’",
   "start": 8.696,
   "end": 12.115
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "text": "And the moment you agree, you feel something strange.",
   "start": 12.674,
   "end": 15.411
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "text": "Not happiness.",
   "start": 16.153,
   "end": 16.852
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "text": "Relief.",
   "start": 17.8,
   "end": 18.186
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "text": "Because, for a few seconds, you know they’re not disappointed in you.",
   "start": 19.021,
   "end": 22.588
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "text": "But what if the thing you’re trying so hard to avoid isn’t disappointing someone, but the feeling that comes afterward?",
   "start": 23.022,
   "end": 28.699
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "text": "You probably know this feeling.",
   "start": 32.541,
   "end": 33.708
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "text": "A coworker asks you to cover a shift.",
   "start": 34.176,
   "end": 36.002
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "text": "You’re exhausted, but you agree.",
   "start": 36.45,
   "end": 38.093
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "text": "A friend calls when you desperately need time alone, and you answer.",
   "start": 38.493,
   "end": 41.944
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "text": "Someone makes a joke that hurts you, and instead of saying anything, you laugh along.",
   "start": 42.395,
   "end": 47.763
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "text": "Later, when you’re alone, you replay the interaction.",
   "start": 48.178,
   "end": 50.724
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "text": "You think about what you should have said.",
   "start": 51.147,
   "end": 52.529
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "text": "You feel frustrated with yourself.",
   "start": 52.967,
   "end": 54.45
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "text": "And the next time it happens, you do the same thing again.",
   "start": 54.946,
   "end": 58.282
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "text": "Why?",
   "start": 59.334,
   "end": 59.991
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "text": "For some people, keeping others happy becomes a way of managing the fear of rejection, conflict, or disapproval.",
   "start": 61.123,
   "end": 66.611
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "text": "The mind learns a pattern.",
   "start": 67.041,
   "end": 68.117
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "text": "If I agree, perhaps they won’t be upset.",
   "start": 68.564,
   "end": 70.763
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "text": "If I help, perhaps they’ll still need me.",
   "start": 71.214,
   "end": 73.142
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "text": "If I never make things difficult, perhaps I won’t lose the relationship.",
   "start": 73.567,
   "end": 77.115
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "text": "And when the other person smiles, you feel relief.",
   "start": 77.626,
   "end": 80.117
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "text": "That relief can reinforce the behavior.",
   "start": 80.647,
   "end": 82.813
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "text": "You learn to reach for approval whenever discomfort appears.",
   "start": 83.256,
   "end": 86.2
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "text": "Eventually, you may stop asking whether you actually want to do something.",
   "start": 86.646,
   "end": 90.083
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "text": "Instead, you ask yourself what will keep everyone happy.",
   "start": 90.543,
   "end": 93.632
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "text": "Imagine that every approving look creates a little light.",
   "start": 94.646,
   "end": 97.5
  },
  {
   "i": 31,
   "text": "You begin chasing those lights.",
   "start": 97.953,
   "end": 99.455
  },
  {
   "i": 32,
   "text": "When someone smiles, you feel worthy.",
   "start": 99.917,
   "end": 102.042
  },
  {
   "i": 33,
   "text": "When someone looks disappointed, you feel as if something is wrong with you.",
   "start": 102.455,
   "end": 105.905
  },
  {
   "i": 34,
   "text": "So you work harder.",
   "start": 106.333,
   "end": 107.149
  },
  {
   "i": 35,
   "text": "You explain yourself.",
   "start": 107.588,
   "end": 108.456
  },
  {
   "i": 36,
   "text": "You apologize even when you haven’t done anything wrong.",
   "start": 108.941,
   "end": 111.967
  },
  {
   "i": 37,
   "text": "You try to repair feelings that may not even be your responsibility to fix.",
   "start": 112.442,
   "end": 116.57
  },
  {
   "i": 38,
   "text": "But there is a problem with building your sense of worth this way.",
   "start": 117.417,
   "end": 119.986
  },
  {
   "i": 39,
   "text": "Other people’s reactions are not under your control.",
   "start": 120.387,
   "end": 122.841
  },
  {
   "i": 40,
   "text": "People can misunderstand you.",
   "start": 123.269,
   "end": 124.563
  },
  {
   "i": 41,
   "text": "They can have a bad day.",
   "start": 124.983,
   "end": 125.934
  },
  {
   "i": 42,
   "text": "They can disagree with you, even when you have done nothing wrong.",
   "start": 126.347,
   "end": 129.354
  },
  {
   "i": 43,
   "text": "And if every negative reaction feels like a verdict on your character, you will never feel completely safe.",
   "start": 129.82,
   "end": 135.349
  },
  {
   "i": 44,
   "text": "There will always be another light to chase.",
   "start": 135.844,
   "end": 137.95
  },
  {
   "i": 45,
   "text": "And while you’re busy chasing those lights, something else begins to happen.",
   "start": 138.401,
   "end": 142.001
  },
  {
   "i": 46,
   "text": "You postpone your own plans.",
   "start": 143.064,
   "end": 144.375
  },
  {
   "i": 47,
   "text": "You ignore your exhaustion.",
   "start": 144.829,
   "end": 146.199
  },
  {
   "i": 48,
   "text": "You hide your opinions.",
   "start": 146.627,
   "end": 147.613
  },
  {
   "i": 49,
   "text": "Sometimes you don’t even know what you want anymore.",
   "start": 148.071,
   "end": 150.138
  },
  {
   "i": 50,
   "text": "You become so familiar with asking what everyone else needs that asking what you need feels strangely uncomfortable.",
   "start": 150.578,
   "end": 156.591
  },
  {
   "i": 51,
   "text": "You might even feel guilty when you finally choose yourself.",
   "start": 157.029,
   "end": 159.789
  },
  {
   "i": 52,
   "text": "And that guilt can be confusing.",
   "start": 160.301,
   "end": 161.724
  },
  {
   "i": 53,
   "text": "You may interpret it as proof that you’ve done something wrong.",
   "start": 162.159,
   "end": 164.606
  },
  {
   "i": 54,
   "text": "But guilt is a feeling, not always a verdict.",
   "start": 165.458,
   "end": 168.073
  },
  {
   "i": 55,
   "text": "Sometimes it appears because you’ve violated your values.",
   "start": 168.533,
   "end": 171.235
  },
  {
   "i": 56,
   "text": "Other times, it appears because you’re doing something unfamiliar.",
   "start": 171.683,
   "end": 174.886
  },
  {
   "i": 57,
   "text": "If you’ve spent years avoiding disappointment, setting a reasonable boundary may feel wrong before it begins to feel natural.",
   "start": 175.386,
   "end": 182.698
  },
  {
   "i": 58,
   "text": "Now imagine a different moment.",
   "start": 184.498,
   "end": 185.914
  },
  {
   "i": 59,
   "text": "Someone asks you for another favor.",
   "start": 186.369,
   "end": 187.964
  },
  {
   "i": 60,
   "text": "You are tired.",
   "start": 188.401,
   "end": 188.977
  },
  {
   "i": 61,
   "text": "You don’t have the energy.",
   "start": 189.426,
   "end": 190.489
  },
  {
   "i": 62,
   "text": "The familiar answer rises to your mouth.",
   "start": 190.907,
   "end": 192.817
  },
  {
   "i": 63,
   "text": "Of course.",
   "start": 193.357,
   "end": 193.864
  },
  {
   "i": 64,
   "text": "But this time, you pause.",
   "start": 195.222,
   "end": 196.291
  },
  {
   "i": 65,
   "text": "You notice the tension in your chest.",
   "start": 196.739,
   "end": 198.264
  },
  {
   "i": 66,
   "text": "You notice the fear that they might be disappointed.",
   "start": 198.793,
   "end": 200.802
  },
  {
   "i": 67,
   "text": "And instead of immediately trying to make that feeling disappear, you allow it to be there.",
   "start": 201.236,
   "end": 204.282
  },
  {
   "i": 68,
   "text": "Then you say:",
   "start": 204.655,
   "end": 205.744
  },
  {
   "i": 69,
   "text": "‘I’m sorry, I can’t today.’",
   "start": 206.892,
   "end": 209.264
  },
  {
   "i": 70,
   "text": "The other person looks disappointed.",
   "start": 211.193,
   "end": 212.722
  },
  {
   "i": 71,
   "text": "And for a moment, you feel the urge to take it back.",
   "start": 213.16,
   "end": 215.817
  },
  {
   "i": 72,
   "text": "You want to explain more.",
   "start": 216.26,
   "end": 217.164
  },
  {
   "i": 73,
   "text": "You want to offer another favor.",
   "start": 217.6,
   "end": 218.856
  },
  {
   "i": 74,
   "text": "You want to make absolutely certain they still like you.",
   "start": 219.301,
   "end": 221.574
  },
  {
   "i": 75,
   "text": "But you wait.",
   "start": 222.904,
   "end": 223.396
  },
  {
   "i": 76,
   "text": "You breathe.",
   "start": 224.335,
   "end": 224.785
  },
  {
   "i": 77,
   "text": "You allow the moment to exist without treating it like an emergency.",
   "start": 226.814,
   "end": 230.255
  },
  {
   "i": 78,
   "text": "Maybe the other person understands.",
   "start": 230.673,
   "end": 232.279
  },
  {
   "i": 79,
   "text": "Maybe they don’t.",
   "start": 232.738,
   "end": 234.304
  },
  {
   "i": 80,
   "text": "Either way, you have learned something important.",
   "start": 234.682,
   "end": 235.902
  },
  {
   "i": 81,
   "text": "Discomfort does not automatically mean danger.",
   "start": 237.249,
   "end": 239.591
  },
  {
   "i": 82,
   "text": "And another person’s disappointment does not automatically mean you have done something wrong.",
   "start": 240.02,
   "end": 244.141
  },
  {
   "i": 83,
   "text": "This doesn’t mean you should stop helping people.",
   "start": 245.708,
   "end": 247.614
  },
  {
   "i": 84,
   "text": "It doesn’t mean every request deserves a no.",
   "start": 248.051,
   "end": 250.424
  },
  {
   "i": 85,
   "text": "And it certainly doesn’t mean you should stop caring.",
   "start": 250.849,
   "end": 252.88
  },
  {
   "i": 86,
   "text": "It means your kindness can become a choice rather than a reflex driven by fear.",
   "start": 253.357,
   "end": 257.507
  },
  {
   "i": 87,
   "text": "You can help because you genuinely want to.",
   "start": 257.954,
   "end": 259.893
  },
  {
   "i": 88,
   "text": "You can listen without becoming responsible for fixing every problem.",
   "start": 260.29,
   "end": 263.768
  },
  {
   "i": 89,
   "text": "You can care about someone’s feelings without allowing those feelings to determine every decision you make.",
   "start": 264.237,
   "end": 269.552
  },
  {
   "i": 90,
   "text": "And when you make a mistake, you can take responsibility without turning yourself into a bad person.",
   "start": 269.998,
   "end": 275.242
  },
  {
   "i": 91,
   "text": "The next time you feel the urge to agree immediately, give yourself a moment.",
   "start": 276.598,
   "end": 280.609
  },
  {
   "i": 92,
   "text": "Ask yourself:",
   "start": 281.058,
   "end": 281.652
  },
  {
   "i": 93,
   "text": "If I knew this person wouldn’t be upset with me, what would I actually choose?",
   "start": 282.125,
   "end": 285.728
  },
  {
   "i": 94,
   "text": "You don’t have to change your entire life today.",
   "start": 286.592,
   "end": 288.609
  },
  {
   "i": 95,
   "text": "You can begin with one honest answer.",
   "start": 289.012,
   "end": 290.646
  },
  {
   "i": 96,
   "text": "One reasonable boundary.",
   "start": 291.092,
   "end": 292.342
  },
  {
   "i": 97,
   "text": "One moment in which you allow someone else to have their feelings without abandoning your own needs.",
   "start": 292.768,
   "end": 297.669
  },
  {
   "i": 98,
   "text": "Because the goal isn’t to become someone who never disappoints anyone.",
   "start": 299.03,
   "end": 302.252
  },
  {
   "i": 99,
   "text": "It’s to become someone who no longer abandons himself just to be liked.",
   "start": 302.711,
   "end": 306.802
  }
 ],
